 "title": "The first 110 letters: “a person can only be considered a spy”",
 "caption": "Letters 1–110 of Mauborgne's cipher of 21 October 1915 (499 letters; the original sheet is lost, the text is Kruh's 1993 printing as given by Futility Closet and Altifina), each deciphered with the key letter of Engineer Field Manual Part V, p. 357, beneath it. No correction applied: the raw output reads “endeazors” at letter 88, marked uncertain.",
 "unit": "letters",
